					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-636741#post-1748858</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-636741/what-lies-ahead#post-1748858</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 08 Apr 2013 16:04:36 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>wishun</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1204404</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Sci-fi Foundation, huh? Very interesting possibilities with that, and this is a solid story to set the scene.</p> <p>Imagine the proliferation of -EX's and associated tech over the centuries, &quot;Any sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from technology&quot; after all. And aliens! We've got two thousand anomalies ourselves, how many does the Begriven Foundation analog have? And how many of ours were utterly normal things to them, or vice versa?</p> <p>Actually, that's an interesting in-universe answer to the Fermi paradox. We don't see all the intelligent life forms that statistics would dictate because most of them don't survive their own crop of xeno-keters long enough to colonize space.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
