				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-636741#post-1737748</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-636741/what-lies-ahead#post-1737748</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 25 Mar 2013 01:57:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>thedeadlymoose</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>732274</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This is fantastic.</p> <p>I really like the excellent detail work, like the Mint Zone and the reading of SCP articles.</p> <p>In terms of nitpicks: You tend to repeat yourself a lot. A good example: &quot;Now he could actually see the Homeworld, the shriveled husk that it was.&quot; and then shortly &quot;Silas looked at the Homeworld for a second, a withered dead ball framed by the light of the sun.&quot; Actually for the latter sentence, you'd already had him looking at the Homeworld for quite a while. (And maybe next time you can learn to fix your own dialogue tags! :P)</p> <p>Also, I'd been kicking around the idea of sci-fi &amp; fantasy versions of the Foundation, and between this &amp; Famine's eggs SCP, we've got an awesome start.</p> <p>(Doctors of the Church &amp; Bellerverse don't count because they don't add in any new, non-Foundation sff stuff beyond a post-apocalyptic future setting.)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
